# TargetHIR P8 migration matrix (unit U7, 2026-11-04).
#
# Source: doc/03_plan/compiler/hir/immutable_hir_p0_mir_inventory_20261103.md
# Plan:   doc/03_plan/compiler/hir/immutable_hir_targethir_mir_refactor_plan_2026-11-03.md (P8, IHIR-04)
# Spec:   test/01_unit/compiler/hir/target_hir_migration_matrix_spec.spl
#
# One row per raw-HIR / target-dependent entrypoint or boundary named in the P0
# inventory. Row format: `id | path:line (P0 baseline 4fccb94e564) | disposition | note`.
# disposition is one of:
#   migrated  - every live caller reads typed TargetHIR; the raw route is unreachable
#   pending   - raw route is still live (a typed reader may exist but is not wired)
#   retained  - deliberately kept on the legacy path (compatibility contract)
#
# HONESTY RULE: a row moves to `migrated` only with live-wiring evidence plus a
# Stage-3 run. PR-D (#6565) landed a typed reader `mir_target_hir_select_arm`
# for the expression arm, but nothing calls it from lowering yet; P4 live wiring
# (asm_and_targets.spl) is in progress. That row is therefore still `pending`.
#
# Default-flip rule: target_hir_mode() default stays `legacy` until
# pending_count == 0 AND the Stage-3 gate (SIMPLE_STAGE3_COMPILER) is set AND a
# Stage-3 qualification run is recorded. Nothing below claims that today.

matrix_version: 1
rows:
  - mir_new_legacy | src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLowering/module_lowering.spl:508 | retained | MirLowering.new unknown-target constructor; compatibility contract, no strict rejection
